; One half of a two-run probe: intern the seal value FIRST, then a second large
; integer, and print the seal's node_inst. Its twin interns them the other way
; round. A kernel whose trivial-int identity is content-addressed prints the same
; number from both runs; a kernel whose identity is a position in a growing table
; does not.
;
; AUTHORED AS .fk ON PURPOSE, against the body's BML-or-higher floor. This unit
; has to be readable by a kernel that has no BML front end — that is the whole
; point of the probe — and those kernels answer a raw `section [form.bml]` block
; with a refusal, not a number. The lowering is the measurement's requirement,
; not a convenience.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk
(do
    (let first (intern_trivial_int 501009504543))
    (let second (intern_trivial_int 999888777666))
    (node_inst first))
